message: "If you use ReproPilot in your research, please cite this software."
title: "ReproPilot: Grounded AI Reproducibility Assessment for Scientific Software"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-07-16
authors:
  - family-names: Anwar
    given-names: Suzan
    affiliation: Philander Smith University
    email: sanwar@philander.edu
repository-code: "https://github.com/szuananwar/ai-assisted-reproducibility-bssw"
url: "https://github.com/szuananwar/ai-assisted-reproducibility-bssw"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - reproducibility
  - scientific software
  - research software engineering
  - high-performance computing
  - grounded AI
  - software quality
abstract: >-
  ReproPilot is an open-source framework for assessing reproducibility
  artifact presence and quality in scientific software repositories.
  It combines deterministic scoring, HPC-aware checks, grounded local
  AI prioritization, benchmarking, statistical analysis, a notebook GUI,
  a web dashboard, and a command-line interface.
